# The ECMA-376 archives the schema-validity suite validates against, pinned by content.
#
# `.github/scripts/fetch-ecma-schemas.sh` downloads each file from
# https://ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/<name> and verifies it against this manifest
# before extracting anything, so a re-upload, a truncated download or a poisoned CI cache is a hard
# failure rather than a silently different schema set. The CI cache is keyed on this file's hash, so
# editing a line here re-fetches automatically.
#
# Part 4 (Transitional) carries the markup schemas: pml.xsd, dml-main.xsd, dml-chart.xsd.
# Part 2 (OPC) carries the packaging schemas: opc-relationships.xsd, opc-contentTypes.xsd.
# Part 1 carries no schema this gate validates against. It is here for the *markup* ECMA publishes
# alongside the schemas — two members of it, both extracted from this one download.
# `OfficeOpenXML-SpreadsheetMLStyles` holds `presetCellStyles.xml` and `presetTableStyles.xml`, the
# only SpreadsheetML markup ECMA publishes and therefore the only evidence, short of a file Office
# wrote, for what a `@theme` position means; `crates/mjx-sml/tests/theme_index.rs` derives the
# mapping from them (MJXOFF-246). `OfficeOpenXML-DrawingMLGeometries` holds
# `presetShapeDefinitions.xml`, which `xtask/tests/published_markup.rs` holds `PresetShapeType`'s
# wire tokens to (MJXOFF-250).
# Part 1 is the largest of the three at 43 MB, almost all of it a PDF the script never extracts; the
# download happens once per cache key, and buying a derived answer with it beats asserting one.
bd25da1109f73762356596918bf5ff8b74a1331642dba5f1c1d1dfc6bed34ecd  ECMA-376-4_5th_edition_december_2016.zip
